			"Message": "build(Sky): Handle VSCode internal imports in Wind output and update config\n\nAdd build-time handling for VSCode internal relative imports that are transitively included through Wind's compiled output. These imports (e.g., ../../../base/common/buffer.js) resolve at runtime but cause Rollup build errors. Added a Vite plugin to stub these imports as external virtual modules during the build to prevent resolution failures.\n\nAlso update import statements and external configuration to properly handle Wind's compiled output tree. Format JSON files for consistency.",
			"SHA": "4ba7a30292ea7c6549cf0eabbbadb5e95016ab9c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-10T13:06:24Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				155,
				3
			],
			"Message": "style(Sky): Add @vite-ignore to Wind dynamic imports and format import statements\n\nAdd `/* @vite-ignore */` comments to dynamic imports from `@codeeditorland/wind` packages in Electron entry points and extension change subscriber. This prevents Vite from attempting to bundle these runtime-loaded modules during build.\n\nAlso reformat multiline import statements for consistency across Electron bootstrap, bundled entry, and extension change subscriber files.",
			"SHA": "6f05fb2a3613f4bb999293f936623b9c6dc6dc2d"
		},
